## Project Overview
Development of a portable Python-based management tool using Streamlit to monitor and modify SmartQuotas across three Dell PowerScale (Isilon) clusters running OneFS 9.12. The tool will run locally on macOS or RHEL, utilizing the official Isilon SDK to provide real-time data and audit logging.

---

## Required Packages
The following Python packages must be installed in a virtual environment:
* isilon-sdk==0.7.0 (Official SDK for OneFS 9.12 PAPI interaction)
* streamlit (Web framework for the user interface)
* pandas (Data manipulation for quota tables and CSV logging)
* urllib3 (Handling SSL/TLS for cluster management IPs)
* python-dotenv (Optional: Managing local session configurations)

---

## System Architecture
* Frontend: Streamlit-based web interface accessed via localhost:8501.
* Backend: Direct HTTPS communication with OneFS Platform API (PAPI) on port 8080.
* Authentication: User-provided Active Directory or local cluster credentials per session.
* Data Persistence: Local JSON for cluster inventory; Local CSV for action logging.

---

